# Intent: Maze (spec docs/design/maze.md, rank 6 of docs/plan/more-games.md; input docs/design/accelerometer-games.md): an 8 by 8 maze made from a seed (a depth first search: exactly one way between two cells), a marble from the top left to the goal at the bottom right, rolling toward the lean of the unit (SF107, roll and pitch in permille) and stopping against walls; You won with the seconds. Two new header-only files: the pure core (it takes the lean as arguments; the maze, the walls, the marble's movement, a solver, an autopilot, the dirty rectangles) and the screen (floor, walls, goal, marble and time chip in ONE draw callback). Registering the game, reading the lean, the 33 ms tick, the sounds (a tick on a wall, ting at the goal), the best time and the game-over call are the firmware track's.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_maze_core.h, maipai_maze.h (new, ours); reads maipai_games_tilt_analog (SF107)
# Check after a flash: Games, Maze: a maze with a pale marble top left and an amber goal bottom right; leaning rolls the marble, a wall stops it, it never passes through; a new maze every game; the goal ends on You won with the seconds.
# Kconfig: none

diff --git a/firmware/main/hal/maipai_maze_core.h b/firmware/main/hal/maipai_maze_core.h
